Z||000006||JAMIE||01-31-2001||04:46 PM||||I have the ACC OEM carpet. It is indeed the correct material. It is jute backed (so it is not exactly a perfect match for an 88 as the 88's had a rubber back - but the fibres are identical to all years for the gray).You should buy an extra yard for the doors -otherwise fading etc will be noticeable next to the floor carpet. Cut pattern is identical to the originals in your car and moulding fratures/points are close to original. Main difference is the heel pads - the ACC carpet has only 1 pad which is on driver side and is stitched on - looks really crappy - the one on mine was even positioned way out of line - your original carpet has 4 pads all heat moulded on.I removed the ACC pad and attached my originals - looks identical to the originals now - took a lot of work to do it though.<P>The guy selling this carpet on ebay goes by the name "partsmonster" - his real name is Kevin - he is reliable and honest.<P>Jamie<P><BR>||||reg||1
